WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.173
^- Peanut butter and jelly.

00:00:07.743 --> 00:00:08.576
- Poo poo.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.233
- Cool, I love having boys!

00:00:13.239 --> 00:00:15.822
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:19.483
Sugar.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.393
Sugar.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.310
Everything has sugar!

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.143
^I'm Hannah.

00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:28.340
^I'm the world's OK-est mom

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.523
and my family has a sugar problem.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.320
Now, I feel like it's my fault

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.750
because I'm a busy working mom

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.280
and I let a lot of things slide,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.320
and I kind of say yes a little bit too much.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.770
So now my kids are expecting treats all the time.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.100
And I feel like their behavior is suffering as a result.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.950
They're not getting good sleep.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.220
And they're throwing a lot of tantrums lately.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.070
Now, I'm not a nutritionist, but I think we can all agree

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.113
that too much sugar is not good for you.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.560
So I want to try something.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.790
For one whole week, I'm gonna cut out all added sugar

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.310
from my family's diets.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.900
Now I'm not saying we're gonna last a whole week.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.020
I'm not saying we're gonna be okay with this.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.410
And we might end up eating each other at the end.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.820
But I'm gonna stay positive and see what happens.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:07.883
So wish us luck!

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.990
So some ground rules for the week

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.033
because sugar is kind of a broad term.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.740
The sugar that we were cutting out

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.760
was added, processed sugar.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.200
We weren't cutting out fruit,

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.850
we're not cutting out fruit juice.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.930
But anything that has sugar added to it,

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.723
or any processed sugar at all was off the table.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.670
So I went specially grocery shopping

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.733
at the beginning of the week for this experiment.

00:01:29.884 --> 00:01:30.717
Goodbye!

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.880
So I am pretty shaken up

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.300
over how much stuff actually has sugar in it.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.800
I felt completely lost in that grocery store

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.883
and I was like, checking every label.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.060
And I'd get through like 90% of the ingredients,

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.193
and then boom, at the bottom, sugar!

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.040
I was very surprised to see just how much has sugar in it

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.960
that I've thrown in my cart and not even thought about.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.160
Like tomato sauce.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.090
When I was looking at the different brands,

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.470
I actually found one that didn't have sugar in it.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:09.663
So had I just taken the time before to check,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:13.180
I wouldn't be purchasing tomato sauce

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.453
^with sugar all this time.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:18.450
^He's upset 'cause he really wanted Kix cereal

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.120
and we're doing cottage cheese and fruit.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.990
Hmm.
- I do not like this.

00:02:23.191 --> 00:02:24.941
- Well, you're eating your oranges.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.003
I'm proud of you.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.643
^Okay, so I totally forgot we have catered lunch today.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:30.883
Nope.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.073
Nope.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.103
I don't know what's on this.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.673
Nope.

00:02:37.673 --> 00:02:39.283
This is my plate.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.173
It looks like a rabbit's plate.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:45.233
This is Allison's plate 'cause she eats meat.

00:02:45.276 --> 00:02:46.109
(laughing)

00:02:46.109 --> 00:02:47.113
But I literally I,

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.200
I'm like not looking forward to this.

00:02:55.613 --> 00:02:57.080
It's like wet kale.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.650
Getting hungry really dawned on me

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.463
that I'm gonna be doing a lot of cooking this week.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.343
^You want dinner?

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.483
^- Sure.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.817
- [Hannah] You wanna eat the broccoli I'm making?

00:03:06.817 --> 00:03:07.650
- No.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.633
- Yes!

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.430
Tonight we're gonna have some roasted broccoli

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:16.940
and some chicken and tri-tip for the boys.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.033
You did pretty good!

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:24.113
Jackson got some broccoli, tri-tip, chicken.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.283
Inside-out PJ shirt.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.903
It is 8 p.m. and we are currently eating.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.200
So in addition to changing my shopping habits,

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.700
I had to change my whole wind down, evening,

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.470
me time, relaxation habits.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.393
I get home from work, we do dinner, get the kids in bed.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.400
And then that's my time to shine.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.133
And I park my butt right here on this couch,

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.033
grab a pint of ice cream, turn on my true crime shows,

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.050
and I just

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:53.913
slug out.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.290
Now, I try to deny this to my kids.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.770
I try to pretend like it doesn't happen.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.883
But they know.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.653
^I'm not eating sugar.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.010
^- [Hannah] No I'm not.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:05.693
^- No.

00:04:05.693 --> 00:04:08.210
So the kids are asleep and this is typically the time

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:11.840
that I would raid the freezer

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.020
and get some ice cream,

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.130
or get some candy.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.900
But I'm not gonna do that.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.293
My body is like, come on, it's time!

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:20.703
But no.

00:04:20.703 --> 00:04:24.593
So I'm gonna eat some kale snacks that my mom gave me.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.700
^So, I made this oatmeal this morning.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.603
^It took forever and I'm gonna throw some blackberries on it.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.450
And that's breakfast!

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.700
I ended up having to make oatmeal from scratch

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.610
because a lot of the packaged oatmeal

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.670
and the instant oatmeal has sugar in it if it's flavored.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.120
- The oatmeal is really good.

00:04:42.134 --> 00:04:43.319
^- [Hannah] Oh my god, you like it?

00:04:43.319 --> 00:04:44.152
^- Yeah!

00:04:44.393 --> 00:04:45.226
^- Nice!

00:04:45.226 --> 00:04:47.370
They were super excited about the oatmeal I made,

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.470
and were like, oh, it's actually good!

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.090
That's some dank oatmeal.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.683
I probably shouldn't say dank.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.880
Dank is done 'cause I said it.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.430
Dank is officially over.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.820
No one can say that anymore.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.393
I'm sorry to the youth.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.770
So very quickly, I realized that at work,

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.670
I needed to bring all of my own food

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.740
because I work at Tasty.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.560
It's the most epic food channel ever

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:11.090
and there's always the most delicious food

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:13.583
just coming out of that kitchen 24/7.

00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:15.840
It's just too tempting with all the snacks,

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.190
and all the catered lunches

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:19.940
and all this delicious food that's always there.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.520
^Nick and I are having our healthy lunches.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.040
- [Nick] Well, mine's not that healthy.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:24.873
- Kind of.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.003
I want dessert!

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.300
I didn't bring a piece of fruit.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.330
I should have brought like a piece of fruit with me.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.670
And I ended up starting to live vicariously

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.253
through my co-workers.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.823
Can you just taste it and tell me how it tastes?

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:38.863
- Yeah.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:39.905
Mm, mm.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.661
- [Hannah] Am I missing out?

00:05:41.661 --> 00:05:42.494
- Yeah.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.720
- There's something really satisfying

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.130
about watching someone else enjoy food.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.870
I'd be like all up in their mouth.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.053
Like let me see.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.580
It's chocolate and white chocolate and shortbread.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.313
Is it good?
- Mm.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:58.190
^- All right, another morning, another breakfast grind

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.453
and lunch grind.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.603
What do you want?

00:06:01.757 --> 00:06:03.223
- I want a cheese quesadilla.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.280
- Jackson has requested oatmeal,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.640
and Wyatt has requested a quesadilla this morning.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.120
So I'm making it because it doesn't have any sugar.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.900
But it's really tough when they each ask

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.113
for something different.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.830
And I have to make two breakfasts.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.690
I'm actually feeling okay today.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.693
My face is a little less puffy.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:22.060
Usually it's really puffy when I wake up.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:25.150
And I think that's partially due to the excessive amount

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.000
of ice cream I eat at night (laughs).

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.180
For me, I have a really big sweet tooth

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:33.590
and I realized throughout this week how much

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.250
I rely on sugar for energy throughout the day.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.060
I am the first one home this evening.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.510
So I'm going to go ahead and start making dinner.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:44.330
Today was pretty difficult

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.370
but I feel like it's getting easier.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.180
Although, I do have a crazy work week this week

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:52.610
and I have noticed that me craving sugar

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:56.300
has kind of clouded my ability to work a little.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.910
'Cause I'm thinking about it a lot more

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.100
and kind of craving it.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.253
But I have a great dinner planned tonight.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.640
I'm making a falafel feast with this flatbread,

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.270
and hummus, and garlic spread,

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.720
and tabboleh, and tzatziki, and olives,

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:10.660
and it's gonna be delicious.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.280
I'm very happy with this dinner.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.640
The kids already ate.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.540
I do feed them, I promise.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.420
^Towards the end of the week, I really thought

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:18.870
^we had jumped over a hurdle.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.140
Like we were on our way and doing great.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.530
But then, I made the mistake of deviating

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.310
from my usual, special oatmeal

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.010
and I decided to make pancakes.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.810
And I used this pancake mix that's, you know,

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:34.053
full of wheat flour, and protein, and no added sugar.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.620
But then when I served 'em, I realized

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.610
I had nothing to put on top of them.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.170
And that did not go over well.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.570
He's crying cause I won't put syrup on his pancakes.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:44.570
(crying)

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:45.633
I'm sorry sweetheart.

00:07:45.908 --> 00:07:47.991
(crying)

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:54.560
So Matt agreed to participate in this experiment as well,

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:55.830
which I was really excited about

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.290
'cause we're all doing it as a family.

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:59.840
Obviously, we eat breakfast and dinner together

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.363
but I wanted him to suffer,

00:08:02.528 --> 00:08:04.233
(laughs) like I was suffering.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:08.500
But I don't know if I quite trust that he followed through

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.523
every day when he was gone at work.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.793
How'd you do today?

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:14.623
- No added sugar.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:17.130
- Oh, really?
- I had a veggie burrito.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:18.560
- Oh, really?
- Mm-hmm.

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:20.893
- Hmm, really?

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.203
In his defense, I didn't make it easy for him.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.523
Do you want ice cream?

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:26.603
Should we cheat?

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.160
- No.
- No?

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.640
- It's been like five days.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:30.623
Let's keep going.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.160
- [Hannah] We have Magnum bars in the freezer.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.753
- Why are you saying this?

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.710
- And just so you guys know

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.360
that I haven't edited this to make myself

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.180
look completely guilt-free

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.793
and like I did this experiment perfectly,

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.653
I have a confession.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.570
^I messed up.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:48.573
^- She cheated!

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.433
^- I messed up, I didn't mean to.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.060
It was totally by accident.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:54.490
I had a co-worker who was like, tasting all these things,

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.220
and she's like, can you taste this

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.300
and tell me if it's spicy?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.890
And I'm like, oh, I love spicy food.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.580
And I put it in my mouth and the second I did

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:04.783
I was like, ah, I can taste the sugar on it!

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:08.260
I just, my hands just grab food if it's offered.

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:10.080
And they just move right to my mouth.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.733
My hands have a mind of their own, okay?

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.673
^Day six.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.260
^Got my eye pads on.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.040
For breakfast we are doing

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:22.643
a totally health food packed smoothie.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.650
Oh, okay.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.270
- Doughnuts, doughnuts!

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:28.940
- [Hannah] No, he's joking!

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:29.963
- I want doughnuts!

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:33.310
- Now, on the final day of this week we had an event.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:36.293
My really good friend's son was turning three.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.270
And she's having a big backyard birthday party for him.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:43.223
There is nothing more tempting, sugar-wise,

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.773
^than a birthday party.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.730
^So we're on the way to the birthday party.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.003
^We have two arguing kids in the back.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.200
So I'm a little nervous because they're already

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.830
in kind of gnarly moods and they haven't napped today.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:55.720
How do you think we're gonna do

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.990
at this birthday party with no sugar?

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.203
- Oh yeah.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.990
To be continued on that.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.300
- So far, so good.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.447
There's a bounce house.

00:10:04.447 --> 00:10:05.307
- There he is.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:06.823
- So, so far, so good.

00:10:07.539 --> 00:10:10.003
At the end of the party, we were doing so well.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.080
We're packing up our stuff to go

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:15.743
and I made the fatal mistake of peeing.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.230
You parents out there know, you can never go

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:21.943
to the bathroom without something horrible happening.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:27.670
Would you take a cupcake out

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.570
of your very temperamental three year old's hands

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.373
at a party with a bunch of other parents?

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.680
Yeah, no, I was not about to go there.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:40.680
But then (laughs), when Wyatt has a cupcake in his hands,

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:42.940
that's not fair to Jackson.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.290
So Jackson needs a cupcake and it just triggered

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.710
this chain of events of, like, ah you get a cupcake,

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:48.543
and you get a cupcake,

00:10:48.543 --> 00:10:50.960
and I had to literally, like, yell at Matt

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.343
to back away from the cake.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:53.213
Think about it.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:54.323
Drop the knife.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:55.813
Walk away.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:57.923
Walk away.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.500
Stop the cupcake cycle!

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:01.333
Like, stop.

00:11:01.333 --> 00:11:02.373
Everybody stop.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:06.230
And here's the kicker of the whole cupcake situation.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.793
While I was in the bathroom,

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.913
Matt was outside with the kids.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.260
Now, I'm not accusing him

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:14.910
of giving Wyatt the cupcake himself.

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:18.003
But all I know is that he assisted in unwrapping it.

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:21.471
- [Matt] Here, buddy.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:27.720
- So, in total, we made it six and 3/4 of a day,

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.210
which is six days longer

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.780
than I really thought we would last.

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:32.210
Good enough.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.400
So in conclusion, my learnings from this week.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:37.000
One of the main reasons why I did this experiment

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.810
is because I was looking to see how it would affect my kids.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:42.210
I was looking at their temperament, their behavior,

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:43.370
and their sleeping habits.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.940
And I definitely saw improvement in all three.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:49.190
They really did seem to have an improved mood

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.480
and more energy and just not crashing

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.223
so much at the end of the day.

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:56.770
Now for me, it kind of had the opposite effect.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:00.020
I was so aware that we weren't eating any sugar,

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.890
it just made me think about it all the time.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.440
And so I felt very distracted throughout the week.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.950
(crunches) I'm really happy.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.043
I love kale.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.513
I love grass.

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:10.190
I kind of envy my kids, 'cause they were,

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:12.660
for the most part, oblivious to this experiment

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:15.040
because they have someone just making food for them.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.440
I kind of wish I had this magic food maker

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.800
who just decided everything I got to eat.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.190
Instead of me just eating a bunch

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:22.713
of cottage cheese all week.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:24.670
So going forward, I really think

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:26.880
that there are a lot of swaps that we can do

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.643
and a lot of things we can be more conscious of.

00:12:28.643 --> 00:12:31.133
Instead of cereal, serving oatmeal.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:34.050
Or instead of packaged fruit bars,

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.480
we'll just eat fresh fruit.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:38.120
I think those are little swaps and little changes

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.200
that are gonna help us long-term.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.210
And I'm definitely gonna be more mindful

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:45.310
shopping in the grocery store to look at the ingredients

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:48.320
and really look for what I'm bringing into our house.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:50.720
Because all of it has freakin' sugar!

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:51.553
All of it!

00:12:52.452 --> 00:12:53.285
Ugh!

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:55.180
So that's all I got for today.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:57.210
I'm Hannah and if you have any tips or tricks

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.860
to get your kids to eat better,

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:00.120
please leave them in the comments.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.530
But be nice to each other, guys.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.800
Because we're all just trying to get by here.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.900
^Or you can text me, this is a real number,

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:07.320
^and I do read each and every one.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:08.820
^I don't always respond because I get a lot

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.673
^but I love hearing what you guys have to say.

00:13:10.673 --> 00:13:12.543
Now, if you'll please excuse me.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.123
My kids are asleep.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:17.510
This is my time to sit on the couch, like the sloth

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.883
that I am and enjoy a box of Girl Scout cookies.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:21.893
Till next time!

00:13:22.119 --> 00:13:24.702
(upbeat music)

00:13:27.942 --> 00:13:29.109
I missed them.

00:13:29.172 --> 00:13:30.255
I missed you!

00:13:36.943 --> 00:13:41.572
Don't look at me! (laughs)

